WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.009
It all started in 2008, when Nick Fury told
Tony Stark about the Avengers Initiative,

00:00:05.009 --> 00:00:09.480
and ten years after Iron Man hit theaters,
Earth's mightiest heroes are set to face their

00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:12.530
toughest challenge: Thanos the Mad Titan.

00:00:12.530 --> 00:00:18.620
Directed by Joe and Anthony Russo, Avengers:
Infinity War will feature at least 76 characters,

00:00:18.620 --> 00:00:23.300
be Marvel's longest movie to date, and revolve
around six mysterious stones.

00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:26.180
Well, seven if you count Deadpool's continuity
gem.

00:00:26.180 --> 00:00:27.490
Which they won't.

00:00:27.490 --> 00:00:28.770
It's a lot to keep track of.

00:00:28.770 --> 00:00:33.170
So if you need a primer to prepare for history's
biggest superhero movie, here's everything

00:00:33.170 --> 00:00:36.940
you need to know before seeing Avengers: Infinity
War.

00:00:36.940 --> 00:00:38.649
Who is Thanos?

00:00:38.649 --> 00:00:42.199
The Mad Titan first appeared in the mid-credits
scene for The Avengers.

00:00:42.199 --> 00:00:46.300
Since then, he's popped up a few other times,
but we haven't really gotten to know the guy.

00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:48.540
What does he want with Earth's mightiest heroes?

00:00:48.540 --> 00:00:51.010
"And who is the man in the purple chair?

00:00:51.010 --> 00:00:54.829
He's purple, he has a magic glove, doesn't
like standing up."

00:00:54.829 --> 00:00:59.420
In the comics, Thanos is a member of the Eternals,
a race of genetically-engineered superhumans

00:00:59.420 --> 00:01:02.390
who colonized Titan, Saturn's largest moon.

00:01:02.390 --> 00:01:07.031
Incredibly intelligent, uber-powerful, and
born deformed thanks to a mutant gene, Thanos

00:01:07.031 --> 00:01:12.010
is absolutely obsessed with Death…the actual
personification of Death.

00:01:12.010 --> 00:01:16.350
Hoping to win her love, Thanos destroys half
the universe with the help of the Infinity

00:01:16.350 --> 00:01:17.350
Gems.

00:01:17.350 --> 00:01:21.140
We don't know how much of that backstory will
play into the film, but it's clear Thanos

00:01:21.140 --> 00:01:25.530
means business, and when he comes to complete
his rock collection, the Mad Titan might teach

00:01:25.530 --> 00:01:27.909
the Avengers what it's like to lose.

00:01:27.909 --> 00:01:29.950
Alien sidekicks

00:01:29.950 --> 00:01:32.850
When Thanos arrives, he'll have plenty of
backup.

00:01:32.850 --> 00:01:37.280
The big baddie has a massive extraterrestrial
army, but he's also bringing his very own

00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:39.740
evil supergroup: the Black Order.

00:01:39.740 --> 00:01:44.280
In the comics, these are Thanos' top generals,
and while there are usually five, it looks

00:01:44.280 --> 00:01:46.960
like we're only getting four in the movie.

00:01:46.960 --> 00:01:48.609
The Infinity Stones

00:01:48.609 --> 00:01:52.580
We know Thanos wants to get his big purple
hands on the Infinity Stones, but what are

00:01:52.580 --> 00:01:53.619
they, exactly?

00:01:53.619 --> 00:01:56.039
We know a bit about their history, thanks
to The Collector.

00:01:56.039 --> 00:02:02.679
"Then the universe exploded into existence,
and the remnants of these systems were forged

00:02:02.679 --> 00:02:05.979
into concentrated ingots."

00:02:05.979 --> 00:02:09.630
As a result, these six stones come equipped
with devastating powers.

00:02:09.630 --> 00:02:11.130
Let's break them down.

00:02:11.130 --> 00:02:15.120
Officially debuting in Captain America: The
First Avenger, the Space Stone is a blue gem

00:02:15.120 --> 00:02:19.570
inside a glowing cube, and it can open portals
across the universe.

00:02:19.570 --> 00:02:23.610
And if the Space Stone lives up to its comic
book potential, then Thanos might gain the

00:02:23.610 --> 00:02:27.190
ability of omnipresence, or being everywhere
at once.

00:02:27.190 --> 00:02:31.030
Then there's the Mind Stone, which powered
Loki's staff in The Avengers.

00:02:31.030 --> 00:02:35.940
Although it looks blue there, the Mind Stone
is actually yellow and can hypnotize and manipulate

00:02:35.940 --> 00:02:36.940
its victims.

00:02:36.940 --> 00:02:40.720
The Power Stone is the purple orb that appeared
in Guardians of the Galaxy.

00:02:40.720 --> 00:02:44.720
It enhances its user's strength and can waste
entire planets.

00:02:44.720 --> 00:02:49.120
In the comics, it also supercharges the rest
of the stones, making them all more powerful.

00:02:49.120 --> 00:02:53.650
Green and stored inside a magical locket,
the Time Stone showed up in Doctor Strange

00:02:53.650 --> 00:02:57.540
and grants its user the ability to reverse
time and create time loops.

00:02:57.540 --> 00:03:00.540
"Dormammu, I've come to bargain!"

00:03:00.540 --> 00:03:03.320
"You cannot do this forever."

00:03:03.500 --> 00:03:04.500
"Actually I can."

00:03:04.840 --> 00:03:07.080
The most perplexing gem is the Reality Stone.

00:03:07.440 --> 00:03:12.020
It debuted in Thor: The Dark World as a sentient
red goo, and while we haven't seen its full

00:03:12.020 --> 00:03:16.620
powers yet, in the comics it can be used to
alter the nature of reality itself.

00:03:16.620 --> 00:03:21.120
There's one final rock that we haven't seen
yet, an orange gem known as the Soul Stone.

00:03:21.120 --> 00:03:25.900
In the comics, this allowed Thanos to control
all living souls and even resurrect deceased

00:03:25.900 --> 00:03:26.920
ones.

00:03:26.920 --> 00:03:28.210
Where are they?

00:03:28.210 --> 00:03:32.170
According to the Infinity War trailers, Thanos
will definitely get the Space Stone and the

00:03:32.170 --> 00:03:33.170
Power Stone.

00:03:33.170 --> 00:03:34.720
So where are the rest of the Stones?

00:03:34.720 --> 00:03:39.490
Doctor Strange placed the Time Stone inside
the magical compound of Kamar-Taj, and following

00:03:39.490 --> 00:03:43.180
the events of Thor: The Dark World, the Reality
Stone was given to the Collector.

00:03:43.180 --> 00:03:47.460
Though after the explosive events of Guardians
of the Galaxy, who knows if he still has it.

00:03:47.460 --> 00:03:50.200
And then there's the Mind Stone, which has
been everywhere.

00:03:50.200 --> 00:03:54.250
In Age of Ultron, the Mind Stone ended up
in Vision's forehead, granting him the ability

00:03:54.250 --> 00:03:57.320
to fly, shoot lasers, and walk through walls.

00:03:57.320 --> 00:03:59.860
As for the Soul Stone, nobody knows where
it's hiding.

00:03:59.860 --> 00:04:04.230
There are plenty of theories being kicked
around — maybe Heimdall has it, maybe it

00:04:04.230 --> 00:04:09.370
won't show up until Avengers 4… or maybe
Thanos has had it all along.

00:04:09.370 --> 00:04:10.790
Torn Avengers

00:04:10.790 --> 00:04:14.530
By the end of Captain America: Civil War,
the Avengers were still split.

00:04:14.530 --> 00:04:18.190
Captain America has given up the shield and
his star-spangled identity and gone on the

00:04:18.190 --> 00:04:19.190
run.

00:04:19.190 --> 00:04:22.570
Tony Stark, on the other hand, is still working
with Vision and War Machine, and the Russo

00:04:22.570 --> 00:04:26.650
brothers promise Infinity War will grapple
with the results of the last Captain America

00:04:26.650 --> 00:04:27.650
movie.

00:04:27.650 --> 00:04:31.371
If the Avengers hope to defeat the Earth's
extraterrestrial threat, they'll have to put

00:04:31.371 --> 00:04:33.760
personal differences aside.

00:04:33.760 --> 00:04:35.320
Guardian grudges

00:04:35.320 --> 00:04:40.430
Star-Lord and his band of misfits will finally
meet the Avengers in Infinity War, and really,

00:04:40.430 --> 00:04:44.500
this battle against Thanos is far more personal
for the Guardians than it is for the rest

00:04:44.500 --> 00:04:46.130
of the heroes.

00:04:46.130 --> 00:04:51.060
Nebula and Gamora were "adopted" by Thanos
as kids and turned into super assassins.

00:04:51.060 --> 00:04:55.130
Nebula has grown up hating Thanos, and getting
revenge against her stepdad is Nebula's number

00:04:55.130 --> 00:04:56.130
one priority.

00:04:56.130 --> 00:05:00.530
"I will hunt my father like a dog and I will
tear him apart slowly.

00:05:00.530 --> 00:05:01.600
Piece by piece."

00:05:01.600 --> 00:05:06.320
Drax the Destroyer is also on the hunt for
Thanos because he had Drax's family slain.

00:05:06.320 --> 00:05:10.660
And with her own dark past involving Thanos,
Gamora isn't a big fan of her adoptive father

00:05:10.660 --> 00:05:11.660
either.

00:05:11.660 --> 00:05:16.270
"When Thanos took my homeworld, he killed
my parents in front of me.

00:05:16.270 --> 00:05:20.410
He tortured me, turned me into a weapon."

00:05:20.410 --> 00:05:21.490
Seeing Scarlet

00:05:21.490 --> 00:05:25.120
Chances are pretty good the Vision won't make
it out of Infinity War alive, considering

00:05:25.120 --> 00:05:29.610
Thanos wants the Mind Stone, and it's lodged
squarely in Vision's forehead.

00:05:29.610 --> 00:05:33.860
The Scarlet Witch also got her psychic powers
from that particular gem, so maybe that's

00:05:33.860 --> 00:05:36.090
why she and Vision get along so well.

00:05:36.090 --> 00:05:40.270
There was definitely romantic tension between
the two in Captain America: Civil War, and

00:05:40.270 --> 00:05:44.010
that might develop into a full-blown romance
for Infinity War.

00:05:44.010 --> 00:05:48.560
Elizabeth Olsen told Nerdist that her Infinity
War performance is her "most emotional arc"

00:05:48.560 --> 00:05:50.080
in an Avengers movie.

00:05:50.080 --> 00:05:52.990
It's a love affair that lines up with the
comics, and it will be interesting to see

00:05:52.990 --> 00:05:57.060
how the two pull off this star-crossed affair,
considering they were on different sides in

00:05:57.060 --> 00:05:58.060
Civil War.

00:05:58.060 --> 00:06:01.550
Of course, their romance will make it way
more painful if the Black Order rips that

00:06:01.550 --> 00:06:04.580
rock out of Vision's head.

00:06:04.580 --> 00:06:05.580
First meeting

00:06:05.580 --> 00:06:10.760
Thor: Ragnarok saw the Hulk and Thor on a
different path from the rest of the Avengers…and

00:06:10.760 --> 00:06:12.600
in a different part of the universe.

00:06:12.600 --> 00:06:15.660
And as the film came to an end, things took
a very dark turn.

00:06:15.660 --> 00:06:18.050
"Meek, where are you from?"

00:06:18.050 --> 00:06:19.330
"Oh, Meek's dead.

00:06:19.330 --> 00:06:22.910
Yeah, no, I accidentally stomped on him on
the bridge."

00:06:22.910 --> 00:06:24.430
Nope, not that.

00:06:24.430 --> 00:06:29.389
In Ragnarok's mid-credits sequence, the Asgardians
were dwarfed by an ominous warship.

00:06:29.389 --> 00:06:35.060
MCU producer Kevin Feige confirmed that the
craft is the Sanctuary II, Thanos' flagship.

00:06:35.060 --> 00:06:38.890
Chances are good that Thanos will capture
the Asgardian ship — probably to steal the

00:06:38.890 --> 00:06:43.010
Space Stone that Loki most likely snatched
from Odin's throne room.

00:06:43.010 --> 00:06:44.010
Home front

00:06:44.010 --> 00:06:49.160
Wakanda was once thought of as a third-world
country, until it turned out to be super high-tech

00:06:49.160 --> 00:06:50.860
thanks to a particular resource.

00:06:50.860 --> 00:06:53.600
"I don't follow, what comes out of Wakanda?"

00:06:55.100 --> 00:06:57.320
"The strongest metal on Earth."

00:06:57.550 --> 00:07:00.960
But why is Wakanda going to play such a pivotal
part in the film?

00:07:00.960 --> 00:07:03.270
Well, get ready for minor spoilers.

00:07:03.270 --> 00:07:07.580
According to Anthony Russo, the Mind Stone
is going to end up in T'Challa's homeland,

00:07:07.580 --> 00:07:11.210
so it makes sense that Thanos and his army
will battle the Avengers and Black Panther's

00:07:11.210 --> 00:07:13.419
warriors on the Wakandan plains.

00:07:13.419 --> 00:07:18.240
Black Panther has also been protecting Steve
Rogers' best friend, Bucky Barnes, since Captain

00:07:18.240 --> 00:07:20.050
America: Civil War.

00:07:20.050 --> 00:07:24.300
Until recently, Bucky has been sleeping in
a hibernation chamber, but in a post-credits

00:07:24.300 --> 00:07:28.600
scene in Black Panther, the newly armed super
soldier was out and about again.

00:07:28.600 --> 00:07:33.220
So when the Wakandans face off against Thanos,
Bucky will be right there with them.

00:07:33.220 --> 00:07:34.220
Missing Avengers

00:07:34.220 --> 00:07:38.790
Avengers: Infinity War is definitely going
to be crowded, and several of the main heroes

00:07:38.790 --> 00:07:41.010
have already been lost in the marketing shuffle.

00:07:41.010 --> 00:07:45.270
Spider-Man and Doctor Strange have both shown
up in the film's trailers, but where exactly

00:07:45.270 --> 00:07:46.949
are Hawkeye and Ant-Man?

00:07:46.949 --> 00:07:51.449
Clint Barton and Scott Lang are pretty big
players in the MCU, but neither have appeared

00:07:51.449 --> 00:07:54.040
in the trailers or on the official poster.

00:07:54.040 --> 00:07:58.090
So have these two Avengers gone AWOL, or will
they help take on the Mad Titan?

00:07:58.090 --> 00:08:01.790
According to the Russo brothers, Hawkeye is
still around, but he's living a different

00:08:01.790 --> 00:08:03.860
life than his superhero buddies.

00:08:03.860 --> 00:08:04.920
As they explained:

00:08:04.920 --> 00:08:07.009
"Hawkeye's on his own journey in this movie.

00:08:07.009 --> 00:08:11.240
[…] He has a unique reaction to the civil
war situation that puts him in a special spot

00:08:11.240 --> 00:08:12.490
in this film."

00:08:12.490 --> 00:08:16.820
As for Ant-Man, Slashfilm reports that he'll
show up in the film, and Paul Rudd is listed

00:08:16.820 --> 00:08:18.460
on the cast list.

00:08:18.460 --> 00:08:22.080
So maybe the tiniest Avenger is lurking in
the trailers somewhere, but we just can't

00:08:22.080 --> 00:08:23.080
spot him.

00:08:23.080 --> 00:08:25.560
He could even be inside someone's suit.

00:08:25.560 --> 00:08:26.880
"Who's speaking?"

00:08:26.880 --> 00:08:28.870
"It's your conscience!

00:08:28.870 --> 00:08:30.610
We don't talk a lot these days."

00:08:30.610 --> 00:08:31.610
Thanks for watching!

00:08:31.610 --> 00:08:34.010
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:08:34.010 --> 00:08:36.119
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

